cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Nexus: an all-mode amateur radio operations center"
message: >-
  If you use Nexus, or the TempoFast or TempoDeep waveforms, in published work,
  please cite it using the metadata below. If your work concerns the protocols
  specifically rather than the application, prefer the protocol reference under
  preferred-citation.
type: software
authors:
  # Amateur radio callsign only, deliberately. The author is identified by
  # callsign in every public surface of this project.
  - name: KD9TAW
    email: kd9taw@protonmail.com
    website: "https://www.qrz.com/db/KD9TAW"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kd9taw/Nexus"
url: "https://hamradiotools.io"
version: 0.21.5
license: GPL-3.0-only
keywords:
  - amateur radio
  - ham radio
  - weak-signal
  - digital modes
  - FT8
  - FT4
  - APRS
  - software-defined radio
  - incremental redundancy
  - hybrid ARQ
  - continuous-phase modulation
  - LDPC
  - propagation
abstract: >-
  Nexus is a free, open-source amateur radio operations center for Windows, Linux
  and Raspberry Pi, written in Rust behind a Tauri shell. It provides an
  FT8/FT4 cockpit with operational parity to WSJT-X, transmit and receive for
  Q65, FST4, FST4W, MSK144, JT65 and WSPR, along with RTTY, SSTV, APRS, CW and
  SSB/FM phone operating, native rig control with RF panadapter streaming, a
  native port of the ITU-R P.533 propagation model, an operator-anchored band
  opening detector, and offline award computation with source-aware
  confirmation tracking. Its digital modem is derived from the WSJT-X DSP
  sources. Nexus additionally implements two original weak-signal waveforms,
  TempoFast and TempoDeep, described in the preferred citation.
preferred-citation:
  type: manual
  title: >-
    The Tempo protocols: TempoFast and TempoDeep, coherent and non-coherent
    weak-signal waveforms with incremental-redundancy hybrid ARQ for amateur
    radio
  authors:
    - name: KD9TAW
      email: kd9taw@protonmail.com
  year: 2026
  url: "https://github.com/kd9taw/Nexus/blob/main/docs/FT1-Protocol.md"
  license: GPL-3.0-only
  abstract: >-
    TempoFast is a coherent 4-ary continuous-phase modulation (4-CPM, h=1/2,
    BT=0.3) waveform on a four-second transmit and receive cycle, sharing the
    WSJT-X 77-bit message payload and LDPC(174,91) forward error correction. It
    is demodulated by iterative turbo equalization, in which a BCJR trellis
    detector for the CPM phase memory exchanges soft information with the LDPC
    decoder. Its distinguishing feature is incremental-redundancy hybrid ARQ:
    retransmissions carry previously unsent parity from a punctured LDPC(348,91)
    mother code and are joint-turbo-combined with the original frame, so a frame
    that fails to decode alone is not discarded. The redundancy version is
    signalled by Costas-array variant and therefore costs no additional bits. No
    other amateur weak-signal text mode accumulates redundancy across
    retransmissions. TempoDeep is a companion non-coherent 8-FSK tier on a
    fifteen-second cycle carrying the same payload, intended for fading paths
    that defeat coherent detection. Both waveforms have closed over-the-air
    links, including a completed two-station contact on the 6 m band. Reported
    sensitivity thresholds are simulation results from AWGN and Rayleigh fading
    sweeps and are not on-air measurements.
